      "writtenOn": "2023-01-03T19:55:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This reads very wrong. SkUnicode doesn\u0027t need to be backed by ICU in order to work. (It could be backed by DirectWrite or CoreText, for example.) What is really being tested for here is that `SkUnicode::Make()` exists and returns a working dynamic SkUnicode object.\n\nThis is basically the wrong place to handle this as a define. `SkUnicode::Make()` should always exist and pick some dynamic implementation if available and return `nullptr` if nothing is available. It should work more like `SkShaper::Make()`. Doing things that way should also mean that there is no reason to export the `SK_UNICODE_ICU_IMPLEMENTATION` define publicly.",
      "revId": "49b0dca6e9eb0e619899b8a8369bbc850c5aee6c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "218df333_d043badd",
